  "purpose": "Determine whether Autobyteus accounts every Codex token-usage update/increment in tool-heavy turns and whether the full normalized usage object contains both per-call and cumulative data.",
  "method": "Monkey-patched CodexThread.recordTurnTokenUsage during live gpt-5.5 Codex runs, sent a baseline turn and a tool-heavy turn requiring separate shell commands, then compared recordTurnTokenUsage calls, full normalized usage objects, websocket TOKEN_USAGE_UPDATED messages, and persisted ledger rows.",
  "result": "The latest full-capture run reproduced the undercount path and preserved the full normalized usage object. Each recordTurnTokenUsage call included raw_usage_json from tokenUsage.last and raw_event_json containing tokenUsage.total, tokenUsage.last, and modelContextWindow. For the tool-heavy turn, three usage updates were received for the same turn; the later two had hadPendingBefore=true. Only the final same-turn payload was persisted/emitted, so earlier last increments were overwritten before ledger accounting.",
